# sha256 pins of the ZiSK proving-key tarballs that zisk-prepare-keys fetches
# from https://storage.googleapis.com/zisk-setup for the pinned ZISK_VERSION.
#
# Polygon publishes only md5 sidecars for these tarballs. The fetch step
# verifies the md5 sidecar AND the pin below; a pin that reads PENDING is
# accepted only with ZISK_KEYS_ALLOW_UNPINNED=1, in which case the step
# prints the digest it observed so it can be recorded here and reviewed.
#
# The 1.3.0-alpha pins were recorded on 2026-09-22 from two independent full
# downloads (the gpu-stack-smoke run 35698097646 with allow_unpinned_keys=true
# and a local stream), both matching the bucket md5 sidecars
# b3d31643958407c9f932e2226d4225e9 and e66e4e927d7561d4e3cd4d1c4752028c
# (tarballs last modified 2026-09-18). Note that the bucket also serves a
# zisk-provingkey-1.3.0-alpha.hash file; its value is NOT the sha256 of the
# tarball and must not be used as a pin. The bucket also holds
# zisk-provingkey-1.3.0-alpha-blake3.tar.gz, the blake3-family key; this
# lane proves under the default Poseidon1 key, the only family with a PLONK
# setup.
#
# Format: <sha256 or PENDING>  <tarball file name>

1e867238e6933c5cc37896d88a344379d29a73af1975c7c741c47be821dfbac2  zisk-provingkey-1.3.0-alpha.tar.gz
092cc6ad0ac1a2b3677ce2bb64ad3c4cf01d6f9aed7c924796ca6612349d9011  zisk-provingkey-plonk-1.3.0-alpha.tar.gz

# History (ZiSK v1.2.0-alpha, retired 2026-09-21; computed 2026-09-09 from
# full downloads whose md5 matched the bucket sidecars):
